/**
 * @mainpage Mod Library Documentation
 *
 * @subsubsection pn Part Number: A0015
 * 
 * @subsubsection contact Contact
 *
 * This library is maintained by the Sun Devil Rocketry Firmware Team.
 *
 * Firmware Team Lead: Nicholas Armistead [@narmistead](https://github.com/NArmistead)
 *
 * Library Maintainer: Eli Sells [@etsells](https://github.com/ETSells)
 * 
 * Copyright Holder: Sun Devil Rocketry (rocketry.asu@gmail.com)
 *
 * @section intro_sec Introduction
 * Welcome to the official documentation page for the mod library. Mod
 * is the platform-independent utility library used by Sun Devil Rocketry
 * for their embedded projects like the Flight Computer and Ground Station.
 * 
 * Most of the utilities in this library are specific to Sun Devil Rocketry's
 * protocols and applications, but we still make an effort to have this library
 * be portable and usable by other people.
 *
 * Mod is split into "components", which are themselves independent libraries that
 * serve a specific purpose. Some components are further split into "modules", such as
 * nav. These modules are cohesive and intended to be implemented together, but are split
 * into modules in order to make the component less complex.
 *
 * @section dependency_sec Dependencies
 * Mod is completely free of external dependencies except for a lightweight 
 * implementation of the C standard library (including math functions, standard defs, and asserts). 
 * Some components are able to be used on their own, and some require other components in this library. 
 * A graph describing the dependency relationships between components is
 * included below.
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph G {
 *     subgraph {
 *         rank=same;
 *         telemetry;
 *         std [label="C Standard Library"];
 *         commands;
 *     }
 *     debug_sdr -> error_sdr;
 *     nav -> math_sdr;
 *     nav -> debug_sdr [style=dashed, label="optional: NAV_ENABLE_DEBUG", fontsize=10];
 *     nav -> std;
 *     error_sdr -> std;
 *     math_sdr -> std;
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * @section quality_sec Quality Assurance
 * Mod is developed at the highest standard of quality assurance at Sun Devil Rocketry. It is used
 * in safety critical projects, so we treat it as such. Our guiding standard is the 
 * [Avionics Software Quality Assurance Standard](https://docs.sundevilrocketry.org/document-control/standards/Avionics%20Software%20Quality%20Assurance%20Standard.pdf),
 * and mod also has some additional practices to ensure software quality, including code coverage requirements
 * from automated testing.
 *
 * The QA artifacts from the latest release of the library will be available at our [documentation site](https://docs.sundevilrocketry.org/document-control/avionics/A0015).
 *
 * @section integ_sec Integration Guide
 * Since each component can be integrated individually, components with integration requirements will have a guide provided in their documentation. The following components
 * work as-is and have no integration requirements:
 * - math_sdr
 *
 * The following components are header-only and therefore only provide definitions:
 * - telemetry
 * - commands
 */